aircondit              package:AA                   R Documentation

Failure Times for Air-Conditioning Units

Description:

     The 'aircondit' data frame has 199 rows and 2 columns.

     Proschan (1963) reported on the times between failures of the 
     air-conditioning equipment in 10 Boeing 720 aircraft. The   
     'aircondit' data frame contains the intervals for the failure time
     (hours) for air-conditioning units in the ten aircraft.

Usage:

     data(aircondit)

Format:

     This data frame contains the following columns:

     'number' the number of aircraft (label from 1 to 10);

     'time' the time interval in hours between successive failures of
          the  air-conditioning equipment.

Source:

     The data were obtained from

     Cox, D.R. and Snell, E.J. (1981).  _Applied Statistics: Principles
     and Examples_.  Chapman & Hall, London.  Example T.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Example 7.5.

     Proschan, F. (1963).  Theoretical explanation of observed
     decreasing failure rate.  _Technometrics_, *5*, 375-383.

Examples:

     data(aircondit)
     plot(time ~ factor(number), data = aircondit, xlab = "aircraft", 
          ylab = "failure time")
